.TH "ROARK\-AGENT\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-agent-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-agent\-create \- Create a new agent
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark agent create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Creates a new agent for the authenticated project.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/agent
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
Name of the agent Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<value>\fR
Description of the agent Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-custom\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
Custom identifier for the agent. Must be unique in the project. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-industry\fR \fI<value>\fR
The industry the agent serves. Picks the default capabilities and industry checks setup adds. One of: HEALTHCARE, FINANCIAL_SERVICES, INSURANCE, DEBT_COLLECTION, RETAIL, TRAVEL_AND_HOSPITALITY, TELECOMMUNICATIONS, TECHNOLOGY, PUBLIC_SECTOR, UTILITIES, LOGISTICS, AUTOMOTIVE, HOME_SERVICES, RESTAURANTS, EDUCATION, OTHER. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-prompt\fR \fI<value>\fR
The agent's system prompt. Setup reads it to decide what to test. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fI<value>\fR
The phone number or connection Roark calls to test the agent Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint.value\fR \fI<value>\fR
Phone number in E.164 format (e.g., +12345678900). Optional when direction is OUTGOING, for an agent that calls from numbers you do not know up front. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint.environment\fR \fI<value>\fR
Environment name (default: production) Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint.direction\fR \fI<value>\fR
Call direction: INCOMING, OUTGOING, or INCOMING_AND_OUTGOING One of: INCOMING, OUTGOING, INCOMING_AND_OUTGOING. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint.outbound\-dial\-type\fR \fI<value>\fR
Outbound dial type: NONE or HTTP_REQUEST (default: NONE) One of: NONE, HTTP_REQUEST. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint.outbound\-dial\-http\-request\-definition\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
ID of the HTTP request definition for outbound dialing (required when outboundDialType is HTTP_REQUEST) Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-website\-url\fR \fI<value>\fR
A page Roark reads to learn about the business. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-testing\-instructions\fR \fI<value>\fR
What you want tested, in your own words. Each scenario you describe becomes a flow. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-setup\fR \fI<value>\fR
Controls the flows, metrics and run plan Roark generates for the agent Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-setup.enabled\fR
Set to false to skip setup. When omitted, setup runs if you pass a prompt, endpoint, website or testing instructions. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-setup.explore\fR \fI<value>\fR
Exploration settings Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-setup.capabilities\fR \fI<value>\fR
The capabilities to test. Omit to let Roark work them out from the agent. One of: APPOINTMENT_BOOKING, FAQ, IDENTITY_VERIFICATION, ACCOUNT_MANAGEMENT, BILLING_AND_PAYMENTS, ORDER_MANAGEMENT, TROUBLESHOOTING, CALL_ROUTING, LEAD_QUALIFICATION, COLLECTIONS, OUTBOUND_CALLING. Repeatable. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark agent create \-\-name <value> \-\-endpoint.direction <value>
.fi
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN\fR
Bearer token used when \-\-token is not given.
.TP
\fBROARK_BASE_URL\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fBROARK_ALLOW_PROJECT_BASE_URL\fR
Trusts a base URL set by a project .roark.json, like \-\-allow\-project\-base\-url.
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Disables colour when set to any value.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
The command succeeded.
.TP
\fB1\fR
The API rejected the request.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command line was wrong.
.TP
\fB3\fR
No credential, or the credential was refused.
.TP
\fB4\fR
The addressed resource does not exist.
.TP
\fB5\fR
The request never completed: connection, timeout, or abort.
